schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-env-faded-chapel
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of the Faded Chapel — Zone 1 of the Twilight Zone. A crumbling
    stone church half-materialized into the boundary between worlds. The nave stretches into
    darkness, its vaulted ceiling cracked open to reveal not sky but swirling deep indigo
    void. Wooden pews line the center aisle but they are dissolving at their edges — the ends
    of each pew become translucent, fading into nothing as if the chapel is being slowly
    erased from existence. Stained glass windows still hold their frames but the images are
    wrong: saints with too many fingers, biblical scenes showing transmutation circles
    instead of halos, figures that seem to watch the viewer. A few amber candles burn in iron
    sconces along the walls, creating pools of warm sickly light that push back the shadows
    but never far enough. Deep shadows pool in corners and beneath the altar — and these
    shadows move when not directly observed. The stone floor has transmutation symbols etched
    into it, faintly glowing amber, as if someone attempted a ritual here long ago. Dust
    motes float in the candlelight. The altar at the far end is split down the middle. The
    mood is sacred space corrupted — a place of worship that has been partially unmade.
    Painterly style, atmospheric lighting, heavy chiaroscuro between amber candlelight and
    indigo shadow.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, intact building, bright sunlight, colorful palette, gothic cathedral ornate, modern church, low detail, flat shading, symmetrical composition"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"

tags: [environment, zone-1, chapel, church, liminal, concept-art, dark-fantasy]
